    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "过 as an experience",
     "texto": [
      "After a verb, **过** indicates that an experience happened at some point: 去过 = «to have been there at some point». To say that it never happened, use **没(有) + verb + 过**.",
      "It doesn't always match the English past simple: **我去过** talks about experience, not necessarily when it happened."
     ],
